===============================================================================
THIRD-PARTY SOFTWARE NOTICES
===============================================================================

The MIT grant above covers the contents of this repository only. Psiphon-3X-UI
installs and orchestrates third-party software that it does not include or
redistribute. Each such component remains governed exclusively by its own
license, reproduced at the URL given below.

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
1. psiphon-tunnel-core — GNU General Public License v3.0
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

    Copyright (c) Psiphon Inc.
    https://github.com/Psiphon-Labs/psiphon-tunnel-core
    License: GPL-3.0
    https://github.com/Psiphon-Labs/psiphon-tunnel-core/blob/master/LICENSE

This repository contains no psiphon-tunnel-core source code and ships no
psiphon-tunnel-core binary. At install time, `installer/psiphon_install.sh`
clones the upstream repository at a pinned release tag on the operator's own
machine and compiles `ConsoleClient` locally with the Go toolchain. The
resulting binary is produced by, and stays on, the operator's server; it is
never published or redistributed by this project.

At run time, the panel and the compiled binary are separate operating-system
processes. The panel supervises them through systemd and communicates with them
only over local SOCKS5 (`127.0.0.1:<port>`); no Psiphon code is linked into,
compiled with, or derived from the Python package in this repository.

The Psiphon network parameters embedded in `panel/psiphon/__init__.py` as
`_PUBLIC_*` constants (propagation channel id, sponsor id, remote server list
URL and its signature public key, and the associated modern fields) are the
public bootstrap values that Psiphon Inc. publishes inside every freely
distributed Psiphon client. They are configuration values, not credentials
issued to this project, and are included so that tunnels establish without
manual setup.

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
2. 3x-ui — GNU General Public License v3.0
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

    Copyright (c) MHSanaei
    https://github.com/MHSanaei/3x-ui
    License: GPL-3.0
    https://github.com/MHSanaei/3x-ui/blob/main/LICENSE

This repository contains no 3x-ui source code and neither installs nor
distributes 3x-ui. The operator installs 3x-ui independently. Psiphon-3X-UI
interacts with an already-running 3x-ui instance exclusively over that
instance's own authenticated HTTP API, on the operator's own server, using
credentials the operator supplies. The verified request and response shapes this
project relies on are documented in `docs/XUI_API.md`.

By extension, Xray-core (https://github.com/XTLS/Xray-core, MPL-2.0) is used
only as it is already installed and managed by 3x-ui. This project does not
bundle, patch, or redistribute it; it writes configuration through the 3x-ui
API.

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
3. Front-end libraries loaded at run time
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

The panel's HTML pages reference the following assets from the jsDelivr CDN:

    Alpine.js          MIT        https://github.com/alpinejs/alpine
    Pico.css           MIT        https://github.com/picocss/pico
    Inter (Fontsource) OFL-1.1    https://github.com/rsms/inter

No copy of any of them is vendored into this repository or into the distributed
wheel; browsers fetch them directly from the CDN at page load.

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
4. Python dependencies
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

The panel's Python dependencies (FastAPI, uvicorn, SQLAlchemy, pydantic, httpx,
bcrypt, itsdangerous, PyYAML, sse-starlette, python-multipart) are installed
from PyPI into a virtual environment at install time and are not vendored here.
Each is distributed under its own license — predominantly MIT, BSD, or Apache
2.0. Run `pip-licenses` inside `/opt/psiphon-3x-ui/venv` for the resolved set.

